specs/hal-engine-architecture/spec.md-217-- `beforeUserInput` receives the content of the last user message ([validated by: receives the last user message content](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L147)).
specs/hal-engine-architecture/spec.md-218-- `beforeUserInput` can modify that message by returning a different string ([validated by: modifies user message when returning different value](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L162)).
specs/hal-engine-architecture/spec.md-219-- `afterUserInput` receives the message as `beforeUserInput` left it, not as the client sent it ([validated by: receives user message after any beforeUserInput modification](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L177)).
specs/hal-engine-architecture/spec.md-220-- `beforeModelResponse` can replace the system prompt, for example loading it from a `PromptStore` ([validated by: replaces system prompt with returned value](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L194)).
specs/hal-engine-architecture/spec.md-221-- `afterModelResponse` receives the collected response text and the usage the provider reported ([validated by: receives collected response text and usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L209)).
specs/hal-engine-architecture/spec.md-222-- `afterModelResponse` does not run when the stream throws, so it never reports a response that was not delivered ([validated by: not called when stream throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L229)).
specs/hal-engine-architecture/spec.md:223:- `onError` receives the session and the error ([validated by: called with session and error when stream fails](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L251)).
specs/hal-engine-architecture/spec.md:224:- `onError` observes rather than handles: the error still propagates to the caller after it returns ([validated by: error still propagates after onError hook](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L273)).
specs/hal-engine-architecture/spec.md-225-- `onToolBudgetExhausted` fires only when the model asks for a tool round the budget refuses: after the last provider call and before `afterModelResponse`, which then receives the hook's sentence at the end of the response text ([validated by: hands afterModelResponse text ending in the sentence, and the usage of a run without the hook](../../src/orchestration/toolBudget.test.ts#L214)).
specs/hal-engine-architecture/spec.md:226:- `afterSession` runs after everything else completes ([validated by: called after everything completes](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L118)).
specs/hal-engine-architecture/spec.md:227:- `afterSession` fires even on error ([validated by: called even when an error occurs](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L128)).
specs/hal-engine-architecture/spec.md-228-
specs/hal-engine-architecture/spec.md-229-A hook receives the full `session` object, so it has access to `session.authHeaders?.authorization` (the caller's bearer token forwarded from the WebSocket upgrade request) and every user message verbatim through `session.entries`; the engine redacts nothing before calling a hook. Anything a hook persists becomes the deployer's own data-retention obligation.
